hfsplus: support S5L8947X per-file encryption and journaled RW mounts

When opening or writing a regular file on an HFS+ volume, check for a
content-protection extended attribute and unwrap its per-file AES-256 key
through the S5L8947X key store helper when available. Decrypt 4 KiB data
fork blocks in hfsplus_read_folio() and encrypt dirty blocks in
hfsplus_writepages() using the unwrapped per-file key and IV key.

Validate and replay HFS+ journals on mount so journaled volumes mount
read-write cleanly without forcing read-only, and mark volumes cleanly
unmounted on both unmount and read-only remount.
---
